dialect protocol
protocol stdio.bmp.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.bmp.op
start op

# P2-FG2: `protocol::OpBinary::encode_op`/`decode_op` (../🦀️component.rs) forward straight to
# `dsl::variants_binary::encode_op`/`decode_op` (🗣️dsl/🦀️component.rs `OpRt` region) -- this was
# ALREADY real binary before this wave touched it, NOT the F6-era `print_op().into_bytes()`
# text-as-binary shortcut this file used to (wrongly) document as a bare JSON payload (confirmed
# by direct reading, not assumed: `encode_op` calls `os_pack::encode_record_body`, never
# `print_op`/serde_json). Same shape as `stdio.txt`/`stdio.zip`'s own already-real mutations
# protocol (`📄txt/…/🧬️mutations/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio`), copied here in shape;
# only `protocol`/`schema` above and the variant ordinal table below differ.
#
# Layout, byte-for-byte, per `variants_binary::encode_op`'s own doc comment (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT`):
# a fixed `format` byte (always `1`), the matched variant's ordinal as a `varint` (declaration
# order, `dsl::DslVariants::variants()`'s own emission order: `NoMutation`=0, `SetSnapshot`=1,
# `SetHeaderFields`=2, `InsertPaletteEntry`=3, `RemovePaletteEntry`=4, `SetPaletteEntry`=5,
# `SetPixelData`=6), then the variant's own field payload, `os_pack::encode_record_body(spec,
# record)` -- itself a varint-prefixed STRING-SYMBOL TABLE followed by a generic, self-
# describing per-field-id TAG+value wire (`🎒️pack/🔢️value/🦀️component.rs`
# `encode_record_body`/`encode_record_fields` -- confirmed by direct reading of a real
# `encode_op(NoMutation)` byte dump). This inner wire is the FRAMEWORK's own generic record-body
# encoding -- shared verbatim by every `#[derive(dsl::DslRecord)]`/`DslOps`/`DslDiff` type in the
# whole repo, not anything specific to `stdio.bmp` -- and is genuinely NOT expressible by this
# dialect's `Array`/`Ref`/`repeat` primitives as they stand today (no dynamic per-field TAG
# dispatch keyed by a runtime field-id, no symbol-table back-reference resolution) -- the SAME
# real limitation `txt-opbinary-record-body-wire-is-framework-generic` (this ticket's own recipe
# §5) already names. Modeled honestly: `format`/`ordinal` are genuinely, individually byte-walked
# and validated; the remaining record-body bytes are one opaque tail -- same "opaque segment only
# where honestly irreducible" carve-out. A framework-level `record-body.protocol.semio`
# description (mirroring M3's own `semio.envelope`/`pack_format` precedent) would let EVERY
# future `DslOps`/`DslDiff`-derived artifact `use` it instead of repeating this opaque-tail
# treatment -- out of this per-artifact ticket's ownership boundary (recorded in `mechanism_gaps`).
framing record
field format u8
field ordinal varint
chain bytes
